<Project>

    <PropertyGroup>
        <VersionPrefix>1.1.0</VersionPrefix>
        <Authors>Erik O'Leary</Authors>
        <Company>Wivuu</Company>
        <Product>Wivuu JsonPolymorphism</Product>
        <Description>Adds System.Text.Json serializer support for polymorphism with a discriminator attribute.</Description>
        <ReleaseNotes>
        - Requires the .NET 10 SDK or later (the generator now targets net10.0); projects can still target any framework.
        - Support C# 15 'closed' base types: unmapped subtypes are a build error (WIVUUJSONPOLY006) and the generated Write switch is exhaustive.
        - Deserialize without an intermediate JsonElement, so each object is no longer buffered into a DOM.
        - Find the discriminator using PropertyNamingPolicy, [JsonPropertyName] and PropertyNameCaseInsensitive.
        - New build error when the discriminator isn't the first property written (WIVUUJSONPOLY007); fix with [JsonPropertyOrder(-1)], or lower its severity in .editorconfig.
        - Support types declared in the global namespace.
        - Non-object JSON for a polymorphic type now throws JsonException.
        </ReleaseNotes>
        <PackageTags>net10;json;serialize;polymorphism</PackageTags>
        <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/wivuu/Wivuu.JsonPolymorphism</PackageProjectUrl>
        <PackageLicenseFile>LICENSE</PackageLicenseFile>
        <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/wivuu/Wivuu.JsonPolymorphism.git</RepositoryUrl>
        <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
        <!-- <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols> -->
        <!-- <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat> -->
    </PropertyGroup>
    
    <ItemGroup>
        <None Include="../LICENSE" Pack="true" Visible="false" PackagePath=""/>
    </ItemGroup>

</Project>